                  title:
                    "Writing a Meeting Request Email: Best Tips and Powerful Examples to Assure Confirmation - NEWOLDSTAMP",
                  snippet:
                    "To write a successful business meeting request email, take the following steps: Make your subject line clear and concise. Provide important details right in the subject line; ... Follow-up before and after the meeting.\nTo write a successful business meeting request email, take the following steps: Make your subject line clear and concise. Provide important details right in the subject line; ... Follow-up before and after the meeting. You might also like: “How to write a polite meeting cancellation email even if it's urgent?”\nThat is why it is essential to give attendees some idea of how long the meeting will last. If there are more than two people attending, include the list of attendees to make the meeting comfortable for both sides. When sending a meeting request by email, it is recommended to start with an introduction and a summary of how you know the person.\nBut what’s the best way to request a meeting? Often, one of the most convenient methods to schedule a meeting with busy business people is email. That way, you don’t catch them when they are distracted or attending to another matter.\nPut this info in your subject so that the recipient can store your email in their inbox and check the date/time without opening it. Don’t add unnecessary things, so that it is fully displayed on mobile devices. ... Indicate whether the meeting will be held in a meeting room or somewhere else. Don’t forget to include an address if you are inviting someone outside of your company. It is also important to include the full date and time of the meeting in the text of your meeting request email.",
