                    "I’m more than happy to answer any questions you may have about my last email. I’d love to reconnect and craft a solution for you. We’re here to help. My inbox is open, and you can also call me at [phone number] to discuss your concerns. ... Sending a message after a meeting is part of building a solid relationship.\nStill waiting on a reply? In 2025, a follow up email can make or break your outreach. Get tactics, examples, and email follow-up hacks that actually work.\nLet’s face it—your prospect probably saw your email, thought, “I’ll reply to this later,” and then immediately got distracted by a cat video or an urgent meeting about an urgent meeting. That’s why follow up emails exist. They’re the polite, strategic way of saying, “Hey, remember me?\nI thought you might like knowing a bit about who we are and why we do what we do. Are you available for a meeting next week?\nI’m more than happy to answer any questions you may have about my last email. I’d love to reconnect and craft a solution for you. We’re here to help. My inbox is open, and you can also call me at [phone number] to discuss your concerns. ... Sending a message after a meeting is part of building a solid relationship.",
